# Rust build artifact
target
.ryo

# Local scratch: task workspace, git worktrees
workspace
.worktrees

# What this repository tells an agent is AGENTS.md, at the root, under the name
# other coding agents read. Claude Code reads CLAUDE.md instead, so the one
# tracked file under .claude/ is a symlink pointing back at AGENTS.md — the
# instructions live in one place and load without anyone wiring them up.
#
# Everything else a session leaves behind is somebody's local state and none of
# it is this repository's to carry. A CLAUDE.md written by hand at the root
# where the symlink could not be made, a personal CLAUDE.local.md, a memory file
# beside whichever crate a session was started in — Claude Code reads one from
# the directory it starts in and every directory above it, so any of them can
# appear anywhere in the tree. `CLAUDE*.md` matches by basename at every depth
# and is what refuses them.
#
# `**/.claude/*` is the same reach for the directory itself: local settings,
# local memory, plugin caches, session state, in a nested .claude/ as well as
# the root one. It is `/*` rather than the bare directory because git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, and the negation has to
# come last — git takes the last matching pattern, so a `CLAUDE*.md` written
# below it would ignore the tracked symlink instead.
#
# The negation is the declaration, and that is the half worth keeping in mind.
# A tracked file that this list refuses reads exactly like somebody's
# `git add -f` past it, and nothing in the result says which it was;
# `!.claude/CLAUDE.md` is this repository saying that path is tracked on
# purpose. It carries weight as well as intent: while the path is in the index
# git consults the index rather than this file, so the file survives either way
# — but the first add is refused without the negation, and so is a re-add after
# `git rm --cached`, or after a Windows checkout writes the link out as a
# regular file and somebody restores it.
#
# Everything a plugin can carry — agents, skills, commands, hooks — is installed
# from the marketplace declared in .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, whose plugin
# sources sit in ./plugins, rather than cloned.
CLAUDE*.md
**/.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md

